## Phase 1: Database Schema (Day 1-2)

### [NEW] `financial_years` Table

```sql
CREATE TABLE IF NOT EXISTS `financial_years` (
    `id` INT(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,
    `title` VARCHAR(50) NOT NULL COMMENT 'e.g. 2024-2025',
    `start_date` DATE NOT NULL,
    `end_date` DATE NOT NULL,
    `is_active` TINYINT(1) NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
    `created_at` TIMESTAMP DEFAULT CURRENT_TIMESTAMP,
    PRIMARY KEY (`id`)
) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8;
```

### [MODIFY] `acc_settings` Table

```sql
ALTER TABLE `acc_settings`
    ADD COLUMN `current_financial_year_id` INT(11) DEFAULT NULL;
```

### [MODIFY] `acc_vouchers` Table

```sql
ALTER TABLE `acc_vouchers`
    ADD COLUMN `financial_year_id` INT(11) DEFAULT NULL,
    ADD INDEX `idx_financial_year` (`financial_year_id`);
```

> [!NOTE]
> `financial_year_id` is **nullable** by design. Existing vouchers will have `NULL` until backfilled. All queries using FY filter will use `AND financial_year_id = X` which naturally excludes NULLs — this is safe because backfill runs before the filter is activated.

